.TH GXWID 1 "2026-09-27" "Peios"
.SH NAME
gxwid \- privileged GXWI listener and PGSS session manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gxwid
.SH DESCRIPTION
Started by peinit. Listens at the registry-configured address and authenticates with PGSS. Sessions use RemoteInteractive tokens and run the configured compositor as the principal.
.PP
The compositor's environment has HOME, SHELL, PATH and GXWI_RUNTIME_DIR, and
GXWI_DISPLAY_NAME: what to call the person, from the authority's profile, or
the account name they logged on as where the profile has none. It is the
first logon's; a session joined again keeps it.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Machine\\Software\\GXWI controls Listen, Compositor, the overlay and Logon text.
.PP
While OverlaySession is set, gxwid runs that program as OverlayUsername and
every request is sent to it, in place of the logon pages and of any session.
gxwid logs the account on through PGSS offering no credential types, so only
an account that needs no credential can be named. The values are watched and
apply without a restart. An overlay that cannot run leaves a page saying the
machine is not ready; the logon pages are not served in its place.
.PP
GXWI's own files, under /.gxwi/, are served while an overlay is up, so an
overlay's page can fetch the logon pages' stylesheet and fonts before it gives
way to them. The logon pages draw a field of stars, and each takes up the
field the page before it left, so the stars carry on from one step to the
next. A page of the same origin can leave its own field for the next logon
page to take up. It stores JSON in sessionStorage under the key
.BR gxwi.field ,
in the shape
.BR "{v: 1, at, w, h, t, glows, stars, rise}" .
.IP \(bu 2
.B at
is the time it was left, from Date.now(). A field older than 15 seconds is
ignored.
.IP \(bu 2
.B w
and
.B h
are the size of the window it was drawn in.
.IP \(bu 2
.B t
is the field's clock in milliseconds.
.IP \(bu 2
.B glows
holds how far, in milliseconds, each of the three glows is into its drift.
.IP \(bu 2
.B stars
holds seven numbers a star, at most 4000 stars: x, y, nearness (0 to 1), phase,
colour (an index into the palette 0 #62d2ff, 1 #c8f1ff, 2 #9d8cff, 3 #4fd1c5),
whether it glints (0 or 1), and brightness (0 to 1).
.IP \(bu 2
.B rise
true has the page's contents rise into place, for a page arriving from one
that was not a logon page.
.PP
Anything malformed is ignored. The numbers are only drawn.
.PP
When a password is sent, the page's card fades while the answer is checked,
leaving the stars for the desktop to take up; if no answer has come within 0.6
seconds, the page says it is signing in.
.PP
The logon pages register a service worker (/.gxwi/sw.js) for the whole
address, so that a page loaded while the machine does not answer is not the
browser's own error. Every request goes to the machine as before; only a page
in the tab that fails, or does not come within 10 seconds, is answered with
the waiting page (/.gxwi/away) kept from when the machine last answered. It
shows the Peios mark pulsing and the machine's hostname, asks the machine
every 1.5 seconds, and loads the page asked for once it answers. Nothing else
is answered from what is kept but the waiting page's stylesheet and fonts, and
never a request made with cache: "no-store". Browsers run service workers only
over HTTPS and on the local machine, so over plain HTTP from elsewhere there is
none.
.PP
New compositor sessions resolve LANG and individual LC_* preferences from
Machine\eSystem\eLocale and Users\e<SID>\eLocale using the authenticated
principal. The fallback is C.UTF-8. Inherited locale overrides are cleared;
rejoining an existing session does not change its environment. Registry locale
preferences are administrator-managed; base-layer permissions are unchanged.
.SH SECURITY
HTTP has no TLS yet. The Experimental image enables TCP 7780 for trusted development networks only.
The SYSTEM service retains SeImpersonatePrivilege to pass an authenticated principal's token to peinit using KACS_SCM_TOKEN. It does not mint principal tokens.

.SH SEE ALSO
The Peios learn documentation and installed registry manuals.
